Stop adaptive scaling when a cluster is scaled manually

Switching "Adaptive" off in the dask-labextension Scale dialog calls
scale_cluster(), which drops the cluster's Adaptive from its bookkeeping
but never stops it. Its periodic callback keeps running and resizes the
cluster over the manually requested number of workers
(CoffeaTeam/coffea-casa#151). Applies to dask-labextension 5.3 - 7.0.

--- a/dask_labextension/manager.py
+++ b/dask_labextension/manager.py
@@ -182,7 +182,11 @@
         if model.get("adapt") is None and model["workers"] == n:
             return model
 
-        # Otherwise, rescale the model.
+        # Otherwise, rescale the model. Stop adaptive scaling first: dropping
+        # it from self._adaptives alone leaves its periodic callback running,
+        # and it would keep resizing the cluster over the requested size.
+        if adaptive is not None:
+            adaptive.stop()
         t = cluster.scale(n)
         if isawaitable(t):
             await t
